<section class="editorial-hero bleed-full editorial-hero--image"><div class="container editorial-hero__inner"><div class="editorial-hero__copy"><p class="kicker">Teen and adult training</p><h1>Make time to train.</h1><div class="editorial-hero__intro"><p>Learn traditional Wado-Ryu in Wroughton or Mevagissey. No previous experience needed: your instructor will guide you through the basics.</p><p>Walk-ins are welcome. Check the timetable and arrive a few minutes early to meet your instructor. You do not need to book.</p></div><a class="cta-button cta-button--primary" href="<?php echo esc_url(home_url('/classes/#class-times')); ?>" data-discover="true">View class times</a></div><figure class="editorial-hero__image editorial-hero__image--full-frame"><?php hakuba_hero_image('images/optimized/cornwall-course-training-2026-1280.webp', 'Hakuba members practising together across the hall at the September 2026 Cornwall course', 1280, 960); ?><?php hakuba_hero_caption('Training together / Cornwall course, September 2026'); ?></figure></div></section><section class="editorial-split"><figure class="editorial-split__image"><img src="<?php echo esc_url(hakuba_asset('images/adult-partner-practice.jpg')); ?>" alt="Adult Hakuba students practising a controlled partner exercise with other pairs training behind them" width="1080" height="1000" loading="lazy"></figure><div class="editorial-split__copy"><p class="kicker">Technique / Practice / Progression</p><h2>Learn the basics. Build from there.</h2><p>Training covers basic techniques, kata and grading preparation. Progress at a steady pace, without pressure to rush.</p><p>Your first class introduces basic movements and dojo etiquette. Wear comfortable training clothes and bring water.</p><a class="cta-button cta-button--secondary" href="<?php echo esc_url(home_url('/beginners')); ?>" data-discover="true">Plan your first class</a></div></section><section class="training-focus" aria-labelledby="adult-training-title"><div class="training-focus__heading"><div><p class="kicker">Fitness / Flexibility / Coordination</p><h2 id="adult-training-title">Start where you are.</h2></div><p>You do not need to be fit, flexible or coordinated to start. Work on each through regular practice.</p></div><dl class="training-focus__list"><div><dt><span aria-hidden="true">01</span>Fitness through practice</dt><dd>Warm-ups, footwork and repeated techniques keep you active. Focus on learning rather than keeping up with someone else.</dd></div><div><dt><span aria-hidden="true">02</span>Flexibility, at your pace</dt><dd>You do not need high kicks to start. Work within your range of movement and discuss any limitations with your instructor before class.</dd></div><div><dt><span aria-hidden="true">03</span>Coordination and balance</dt><dd>Practise foot placement, stances and linking movements. Repetition helps you work on balance and control, not just speed.</dd></div></dl></section><section id="women-starting-karate" class="editorial-band bleed-full"><div class="container editorial-band__inner"><div><p class="kicker">Women starting karate</p><h2>A first class.<br>Not a fitness test.</h2><p>You do not need a sporting background to give karate a go. Women are welcome in Hakuba's mixed teen and adult sessions, including complete beginners.</p><a class="cta-button cta-button--primary" href="<?php echo esc_url(home_url('/contact?interest=Beginner')); ?>" data-discover="true">Questions about starting?</a></div><div><h3>Questions before you start?</h3><p>If you would like to ask about the pace or partner practice, you can contact us before visiting or speak to your instructor when you arrive. We can explain what to expect and help you choose a suitable session.</p><h3>What you will learn</h3><p>Learn basic techniques, kata and controlled partner exercises, with guidance from your instructor.</p><p>These are mixed classes, not a separate women-only course.</p></div></div></section><?php hakuba_class_link(); ?><section><h2>Choose your dojo.</h2><p>Choose a teen, adult or mixed session at Wroughton, or the family and adults session at Mevagissey. The class timetable is maintained by the club.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="cta-button cta-button--primary" href="<?php echo esc_url(home_url('/classes/adults')); ?>" data-discover="true">Adult session details</a><a class="cta-button cta-button--secondary" href="<?php echo esc_url(home_url('/locations')); ?>" data-discover="true">Find your venue</a></div></section><section class="pathway-split"><article><p class="kicker">Between classes</p><h2>Revisit what you learn.</h2><p>The public grading syllabus and karate terminology are useful references alongside your instructor's guidance.</p><div class="button-row"><a href="https://hakuba-karate.co.uk/grading-syllabus/" class="cta-button cta-button--secondary">Grading syllabus</a><a href="https://hakuba-karate.co.uk/karate-terminology/" class="cta-button cta-button--secondary">Karate terminology</a></div></article><article><p class="kicker">For club members</p><h2>Training references in one place.</h2><p>The member app is for registered, club-approved members and requires sign-in. You do not need it to attend your first class or ask a question.</p><a class="cta-button cta-button--secondary" href="<?php echo esc_url(home_url('/app')); ?>" data-discover="true">About the member app</a></article></section><section><h2>Before your first adult class</h2><details class="faq-item"><summary>Can I start with no martial arts experience?</summary><p>Yes. Beginners start with the fundamentals, including basic movements and dojo etiquette. You do not need to know Japanese terms, own a gi or have held a belt before.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Are these women-only classes?</summary><p>No. Women are welcome in our mixed teen and adult classes. Tell us if you are nervous about starting or have questions about partner work so we can discuss your first visit.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>What should I wear?</summary><p>Comfortable training clothing is enough for your first class. Bring water and arrive a few minutes early to meet your instructor. You do not need to book.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>How do I work towards a belt?</summary><p>Use the published grading syllabus alongside your instructor's guidance. Gradings mark your progress; you do not need to prepare for one before your first lesson.</p></details></section><section class="join-band bleed-full"><div class="container join-band__inner"><div><p class="kicker">Wroughton / Mevagissey</p><h2>Ready for your first class?</h2><p>Choose a teen or adult session and arrive a few minutes early. No booking needed. Beginners are welcome at the club from age 7; if you need help choosing a class, tell us the student's age and preferred dojo.</p></div><a class="cta-button cta-button--primary" href="<?php echo esc_url(home_url('/classes/#class-times')); ?>" data-discover="true">View class times <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a></div></section>
